+        // A wake-up can race with the end of the task: the waker marks the task as woken, the
+        // task runs to its end anyway, and `exit_current` dequeues it and clears its CPU. Put
+        // back in a run queue, the task would return from `exit_current` when picked again.
+        // Holding the CPU of the task now, the waker sees that it finished.
+        if task.is_finished() {
+            task.cpu().set_to_none();
+            return None;
+        }
+
         // Preempt if the new task has a higher priority.
         let should_preempt = rq
             .current
